IN THE HIGH COURT OF DELHI
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 3490 of 2020
CITATION: 2020 SCC OnLine Del 2068
YEAR: 2020

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Prathiba M. Singh

PARTIES:
Halliburton Offshore vs Vedanta Ltd

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Indian Contract Act, 1872

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 56 Contract Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
covid-19 force majeure, bank guarantee invocation, contract performance

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that Covid-19 pandemic cannot be used as an automatic excuse to escape contractual performance or restrain invocation of unconditional bank guarantees.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 56 Contract Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

